# The ISS's TRRJ radiators at the moment of issue 20261020_214656 ("advance time here, the radiators totally flip"):
# with joint mode edge_on they swapped to the other edge-on solution 20 s after the shot (a 179-degree jump of the
# radiators group, harness `joints`); edge_on_continuous (2026-10-20) keeps one solution, turning once per orbit.
# The camera rides beside the station (follow, cross-track), captures every 10 s through the old flip.
#   python tools/harness/run.py tools/harness/scripts/iss_radiators.satcmd
time set 2027-08-30T11:01:04Z
time pause
select const "International Space Station"
follow offset=10,-120,15
follow aim=sat
joints minutes=280 step=20
wait settle
wait 30
capture rad_t00
time add 10; wait 4; capture rad_t10
time add 10; wait 4; capture rad_t20
time add 10; wait 4; capture rad_t30
time add 10; wait 4; capture rad_t40
time add 600; wait 4; capture rad_t640
time add 1200; wait 4; capture rad_t1840
